id: CTB-SRC0015-8-1
source: SRC-0015
section: §8.1
kind: requirement
extends: LXM-REQ-000043
text: Demonstrate that: The governance core has no closed list of technology categories. Technology definitions and supported categories can be registered through extensible contracts. New releases can be discovered without manually editing multiple version lists. Compatibility and security are evaluated before approval. Build and deployment configuration is generated or validated against canonical resolutions. Drift, unsupported versions, deprecation and security issues are detected. A representative new tool can be registered through the existing mechanism without creating a competing governance system. Truly new protocols or behaviors have a documented, controlled adapter-extension path. The complete governance lifecycle is auditable and reproducible. All claims are supported by tests and repository evidence.
